course: dictionary
lesson: 15169
title: Screaming: loud words in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Screaming means shouting very loudly in a high voice. People scream when they are scared, hurt, angry or very excited. «The girl was screaming on the roller coaster as it dropped.» The drop and the fast ride are clues, so screaming here shows fear or excitement.
explain: Screaming can also describe a loud, high noise made by a thing, like brakes or wind. «The brakes were screaming as the bus stopped.» Brakes cannot shout, so the word is describing the sound they make.
explain: In informal speech, screaming can describe something very bright or very strong. «Her socks were screaming pink.» Socks cannot shout, so the word means very bright. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Screaming means shouting very loudly in a high voice.
fact: «Screaming» can describe a loud, high noise, like brakes or wind.
fact: Informal: «screaming colours» means very bright colours.
fact: «Kicking and screaming» means going somewhere unwillingly, while fighting against it.
fact: In real danger, screaming «Help!» is a way to get people's attention.
exercise: «The children were screaming with laughter at the clown.» What does screaming mean here? | Sleeping soundly | *Laughing very loudly | Running very fast | Crying quietly
exercise: «The brakes were screaming as the car stopped.» What is screaming describing? | *A loud, high noise | A quiet whisper | A happy song | A bright colour
exercise: «Her shoes were screaming pink.» What does screaming mean in this sentence? | *Very bright and strong | Very quiet | Very cold
exercise: Lena says screaming always means someone is shouting. Is she right? | No, it can also describe a loud noise like brakes | Yes, screaming only ever means a person shouting | *No, it can also describe a loud noise like brakes, and a bright colour
test: Why is screaming «Help!» useful if you are in danger? | *It gets people's attention quickly | It is only good for singing | It makes you quieter | It makes the danger go away by itself
test: «The baby was screaming in the shop.» What is the most likely feeling behind the screaming? | Very happy and calm | Sleepy and bored | *Upset or in pain | Whispering a secret
exam: «He was kicking and screaming when they took him to the dentist.» What does kicking and screaming suggest? | He was asleep | *He did not want to go | He was very quiet | He was happy to go
